Package: libsdl3-ttf0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# Was libsdl3-ttf-0 before this was published to a PPA, which is not the name
# Debian and Ubuntu use for this SONAME. Anyone who installed the .deb files
# from a GitHub release has the old name, and both packages ship the same
# files, so an upgrade needs these two to replace it rather than collide.
Conflicts: libsdl3-ttf-0
Replaces: libsdl3-ttf-0
Description: SDL3_ttf TrueType font rendering library (shared library)
 SDL3_ttf is an add-on for SDL 3 that renders TrueType fonts to SDL surfaces
 and textures, with text shaping through HarfBuzz and colour emoji through
 plutosvg.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libsdl3-ttf-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: libsdl3-ttf0 (= ${binary:Version}), libsdl3-dev, libplutosvg-dev,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: SDL3_ttf TrueType font rendering library (development files)
 SDL3_ttf is an add-on for SDL 3 that renders TrueType fonts to SDL surfaces
 and textures, with text shaping through HarfBuzz and colour emoji through
 plutosvg.
 .
 This package contains the headers, pkg-config and CMake files needed to build
 against it.

Package: libplutosvg0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# Renamed from libplutosvg-0 for the same reason as the SDL satellites: a
# SONAME ending in a letter takes the version with no separator.
Conflicts: libplutosvg-0
Replaces: libplutosvg-0
Description: plutosvg and plutovg (shared libraries)
 plutosvg renders SVG documents, including the OpenType-SVG glyphs used for
 colour emoji, on top of the plutovg canvas. Built here with its FreeType
 integration, which is what SDL3_ttf uses.
 .
 Neither library is packaged for Debian or Ubuntu. One build produces both and
 they are versioned together, so they ship as a single package pair.
 .
 This package contains the shared libraries.

Package: libplutosvg-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: libplutosvg0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: plutosvg and plutovg (development files)
 plutosvg renders SVG documents, including the OpenType-SVG glyphs used for
 colour emoji, on top of the plutovg canvas. Built here with its FreeType
 integration, which is what SDL3_ttf uses.
 .
 This package contains the headers, pkg-config and CMake files needed to build
 against it.
